{"id": "EUVD-2026-103709", "enisaUuid": "0d03681b-f117-3f73-8f17-3106844e8269", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Fix AArch32 DBGBXVR<n> handling\n\nThe consolidation of the breakpoint and watchpoint register accessors\nswitched DBGBXVR<n> from trap_bvr() to trap_dbg_wb_reg(). The latter\nselects backing storage with demux_wb_reg(), which only handles Op2 values\n4 through 7. Since DBGBXVR<n> uses Op2 1, an AArch32 guest access hits\nKVM_BUG_ON() and marks the VM dead.\n\nDBGBXVR<n> aliases DBGBVR<n>_EL1[63:32], and its AA32(HI) descriptor\nalready selects the upper half. Map Op2 1 to dbg_bvr[] alongside Op2 4,\nrestoring the pre-regression behavior.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8530a05b304d312fe7dfbc5df7d3e87cc31b256a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af6813d16ace2765011ca1c567be86ade1d1ee8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b1bca1b1ab77f60a62087337bfe6e2f0efb9e6d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98469", "GHSA-vcw8-qqhm-h682"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c476e9b-f91b-3a2b-8864-6d80c1074a97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3ce9f3357e9e099f02feaa002769eb99ef1138cd <6b1bca1b1ab77f60a62087337bfe6e2f0efb9e6d"}, {"id": "11a693d6-d4ca-3fe5-a735-f7b882b9906a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3ce9f3357e9e099f02feaa002769eb99ef1138cd <8530a05b304d312fe7dfbc5df7d3e87cc31b256a"}, {"id": "456496ba-bd42-30b7-93bf-8a8f79c07e29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "8b8ce599-f1f3-3253-b567-662bdb6412e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "9b60b56f-39cb-3404-b93d-b4397d5f5aaa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": 